menu "esp-vim network"

    choice ESP_VIM_NET
        prompt "Network interface"
        default ESP_VIM_NET_WIFI if SOC_WIFI_SUPPORTED
        default ESP_VIM_NET_ETH if SOC_EMAC_SUPPORTED
        default ESP_VIM_NET_NONE
        help
            How the device reaches the network. WiFi (native on the ESP32-S3,
            through the ESP32-C6 on the Tab5) is added in Phase 6f.

        config ESP_VIM_NET_NONE
            bool "None"

        config ESP_VIM_NET_WIFI
            bool "WiFi (the chip's own radio)"
            depends on SOC_WIFI_SUPPORTED
            help
                Station mode. :EspWifiConnect stores the network in NVS and the
                device reconnects at every boot. esp-emu provides a soft AP
                (myssid / mypassword) for testing.

        config ESP_VIM_NET_ETH
            bool "Ethernet (internal EMAC, generic IEEE 802.3 PHY)"
            depends on SOC_EMAC_SUPPORTED
            help
                The ESP32-P4's EMAC. This is also what esp-emu models, so the
                P4 build has networking in the emulator (--net user). A board
                with no Ethernet PHY simply never gets a link.
    endchoice

endmenu
